message: "If you use this software in academic research or educational coursework, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Cheminformatics Explorer: Keyless Client-Side Chemical Space Workbench"
version: 1.0.1
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23418253
date-released: 2026-10-16
authors:
  - family-names: Karmakar
    given-names: Asmita
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-4710-5237"
    email: "karmakarasmita147@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/asmita-ai/cheminformatics-explorer"
url: "https://asmita-ai.github.io/cheminformatics-explorer/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Cheminformatics Explorer is a client-side, keyless web application designed
  for chemistry students, researchers, and educators. It integrates real-time
  3D molecular conformations (3Dmol.js), 2D structure graphs and SMARTS functional
  group matching (RDKit.js WASM), oral drug-likeness evaluation (Lipinski Rule of 5,
  Veber criteria, Crippen logP vs XLogP3-AA), medicinal chemistry structural alerts
  (PAINS and Brenk filters), GHS laboratory safety hazard classifications, and
  chemical ontology annotations (ChEBI and ChEMBL) with honest scientific provenance labeling.
notes: >-
  This tool was conceived, directed and scientifically validated by Asmita Karmakar, an M.Sc. Chemistry graduate. As the author has no formal programming background, the source code was written with the assistance of generative AI tools under the author's direction. The author defined the scope, selected the data sources, reviewed the outputs and checked results against reference compounds in PubChem. The author is responsible for the content. Errors may remain; please report them at https://github.com/asmita-ai/cheminformatics-explorer/issues
